Adapted Core files: data.py, helpers.py, sensor.py, validate.py, types.py.
Changes: independent location managers and storage, location-namespaced cost
and transform sensors, explicit manager lookup, task-local validation cost
maps, config-entry sensor setup, durable saves and listener cleanup.
tools/vendor_core.py reproduces the adaptations from retained upstream files.

Native panels, configuration and shared controls are loaded from the user's
installed Home Assistant. A generator-aware adaptation of the Energy cards,
strategies and calculations is bundled from frontend commit
a67b691a451e0b3fc469679b07158f963a61842c (20261028.4).
tools/build-native.mjs records the adaptations; upstream/frontend-extension.json
records source hashes. Bundled dependency licenses are in frontend/native-licenses.txt.
Internal interfaces require testing against the installed frontend/Core version.

This is an independent community extension, not an official Home Assistant product.
